<title>SINGAPORE: Metro 1st-half net back into profit.</title>
<headline>Metro 1st-half net back into profit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>(millions of Singapore dollars unless specified)</p>
<p>    Net profit				  2.47  vs  1.12 (loss)</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share (cts)	2.34 vs   1.06 (loss)</p>
<p>    Turnover				  105.63 vs 103.67</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	   0.06 vs   0.55</p>
<p>    Operating profit			 12.26 vs   9.73</p>
<p>    Interest expense			  3.60 vs   3.94</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	     2.00 vs   2.52</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			    6.66 vs   3.27</p>
<p>    Loss from associates		    0.62 vs   2.73</p>
<p>    Tax					   3.54 vs   1.70</p>
<p>    Minorities		     (loss)   0.03 vs   0.04 (gain)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		(gain)   0.19 vs    nil</p>
<p>Note - Metro Holdings Ltd owns a chain of department stores.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
